The current directory contains:
- {{ release_note_file }} (Release Note — each task has a task_id and GitHub context)
- {{ code_diff_file }} (Code Diff)
- output.json (pre-filled with all task_id keys as empty lists, plus "doc" and "others")

Analyze the library update between two versions of a codebase, based on the Release Note and the CodeDiff. Map each diff hunk to the task_id(s) it supports. Write the result to output.json.

Rules:
- A hunk is identified by its @@ header up to and including the closing @@. Do NOT include trailing context (e.g. "@@ -185,6 +185,15 @@" not "@@ -185,6 +185,15 @@ class Foo:").
- A hunk can match multiple tasks (multi-label).
- "doc": purely documentation/comments/type-only changes with no runtime effect.
- "others": does not match any task.
- Every hunk must be assigned. Do NOT leave any unmatched.

Output format — each task_id maps to a list of: {"header": "diff --git a/... b/...", "hunks": ["@@ -a,b +c,d @@", ...]}
